From: Inesh Dey <79165198+ineshd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] macOS: MAP_JIT write toggle for unaligned atomic backpatching

HandleUnalignedAccess takes the spinlock in the block's JITCodeTail and rewrites
the faulting instruction. Both live in the code buffer, which HB_FEX_MAPJIT=1
maps as MAP_JIT, so a thread may write them only between HbJitWrite(true) and
HbJitWrite(false). Patch 0033 wraps the other code-buffer writers but not this
one, so the first unaligned STLUR/LDAPUR/STLR/LDAR in a block faults on the lock.

The guard is declared before the lock so it is destroyed after it: the unlock is
also a write to the code buffer.

Compiled for arm64ec with llvm-mingw 20260922 on FEX 2610 plus 0001 to 0033. Not yet tested in game.
---
 FEXCore/Source/Utils/ArchHelpers/Arm64.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Utils/ArchHelpers/Arm64.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Utils/ArchHelpers/Arm64.cpp
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Utils/ArchHelpers/Arm64.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Utils/ArchHelpers/Arm64.cpp
@@ -2103,6 +2103,12 @@
   // Lock code mutex during any SIGBUS handling that potentially changes code.
   // Due to code buffer sharing between threads, code must be carefully backpatched from last to first.
   // Multiple threads can be attempting to handle the SIGBUS or even be executing the code being backpatched.
+  struct HbJitWriteScope {
+    HbJitWriteScope() { FEXCore::Context::HbJitWrite(true); }
+    ~HbJitWriteScope() { FEXCore::Context::HbJitWrite(false); }
+  };
+  // Before lk: the lock and the patched instructions are in the MAP_JIT code buffer, and so is the unlock.
+  HbJitWriteScope JitWrite;
   FEXCore::Utils::SpinWaitLock::UniqueSpinMutex lk(&InlineTail->SpinLockFutex);

   if ((Instr & LDAXR_MASK) == LDAR_INST ||  // LDAR*
